{
 "slug": "js_regexp",
 "course": "js",
 "order": 81,
 "url": "/js/js_regexp.asp",
 "title": "JavaScript RegExp",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "JavaScript RegExp"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Regular Expressions"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "A Regular Expression is a sequence of characters that forms a search pattern."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Regex is a common shorthand for a regular expression."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "JavaScript RegExp is an Object for handling Regular Expressions."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "RegExp are be used for:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Text searching",
    "Text replacing",
    "Text validation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Visit W3Schools\";\n\nlet n = text.search(/w3schools/i);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_string_search"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Example explained:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "/w3schools/i  is a regular expression."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "w3schools  is a pattern (to be used in a search)."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "i  is a modifier (modifies the search to be case-insensitive)."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Regular Expression Syntax"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "/pattern/modifier flags"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using String Methods"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Regular expressions are often used with the string methods:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Method",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "match(regex)",
     "Returns an Array of results"
    ],
    [
     "replace(regex)",
     "Returns a new String"
    ],
    [
     "search(regex)",
     "Returns the index of the first match"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using String match()"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Visit W3Schools\";\n\nlet n = text.match(/W3schools/);",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_method_match"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using String replace()"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Visit Microsoft!\";\n\nlet result = text.replace(/Microsoft/i, \"W3Schools\");",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_method_replace"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using String search()"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Visit W3Schools\";\n\nlet n = text.search(/W3Schools/);",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_method_search"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "RexExp Alternation (OR)"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "In a regular expression an alternation is denoted with a vertical line character |."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "An alternation matches any of the alternatives separated with |."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Black, white, red, green, blue, yellow.\";\n\nlet result = text.match(/red|green|blue/g);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_xy"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript Regex Flags"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "/pattern/flags",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Regular expression flags are parameters that can modify how a pattern is used,\nsuch as making it case-insensitive or global."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "These are the most common:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Flag",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "/g",
     "Performs a global match (find all)"
    ],
    [
     "/i",
     "Performs case-insensitive matching"
    ],
    [
     "/u",
     "Enables Unicode support (new 2015)"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The /g Flag (Global)"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The /g flag matches all occurrences of the pattern, rather than just the first one."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Is this all there is?\";\n\nconst pattern = /is/g;\n\nlet result = text.match(pattern);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_g"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The /i Flag (Insensitive)"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The /i flag makes a match case-insensitive: /abc/i matches \"abc\", \"AbC\", \"ABC\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Visit W3Schools\";\n\nconst pattern = /w3schools/i;\n\nlet result = text.match(pattern);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_i"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Learn More:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "JavaScript RegExp Flags"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "RexExp Metacharacters"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "// Match words\n\nconst pattern = /\\w/;",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Metacharacters are characters with a special meaning."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "They can be used to match digits, words, spaces, and more."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "These are the most common:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Meta",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "\\d",
     "Matches Digits"
    ],
    [
     "\\w",
     "Matches Words"
    ],
    [
     "\\s",
     "Matches Spaces"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "RegExp \\d (digits) Metacharacter"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The \\d metacharacter matches digits."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Give 100%!\";\n\nconst pattern = /\\d/g;\n\nlet result = text.match(pattern);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_d"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "RegExp \\w (word) Metacharacter"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The \\w metacharacter matches word characters."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "A word character is a character a-z, A-Z, 0-9, including _ (underscore)."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"Give 100%!\";\n\nconst pattern = /\\w/g;\n\nlet result = text.match(pattern);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_wordchar"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Learn More:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "JavaScript RegExp Metacharacters"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript RegExp Quantifiers"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Quantifiers define the numbers of characters or expressions to match."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const pattern = /lo+/;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The + means \"one or more\". The pattern matches:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "lo",
    "loo",
    "looo"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "These are the most common quantifiers:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Quantifier",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "x+",
     "Matches any string with at least one occurrences of x"
    ],
    [
     "x*",
     "Matches any string with zero or more occurrences of x"
    ],
    [
     "x?",
     "Matches any string with zero or one occurrences of x"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The ? Quantifier"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "x? matches zero or one occurrences of x."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"1, 100 or 1000?\";\n\nconst pattern = /10?/g;\n\nlet result = text.match(pattern);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_n3"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Learn More:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "JavaScript RegExp Quantifiers"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Regular Expression Assertions"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "// Match beginning of string\n\nconst pattern = /^W3Schools/;\n\n// Match end of string\n\nconst pattern = /W3Schools$/;",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Assertions matches Boundaries and Lookarounds:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "String Boundaries and Word Boundaries."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Lookarounds: Lookaheads and Lookbehinds."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "These are the most common:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Syntax",
     "Name",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "^",
     "String boundary",
     "Matches the beginning of a string"
    ],
    [
     "$",
     "String boundary",
     "Matches the end of a string"
    ],
    [
     "\\b",
     "Word boundary",
     "Matches the beginning or end of a word"
    ],
    [
     "(?=...)",
     "Lookahead",
     "Matches the subsequent string"
    ],
    [
     "(?<=...)",
     "Lookbehind",
     "Matches the previous string"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "RegExp ^ Metacharacter"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The ^ metacharacter matches the beginning of a string."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const pattern = /^W3Schools/;\n\nlet text = \"W3Schools Tutorial\";\n\nlet result = pattern.test(text); // true",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const pattern = /^W3Schools/;\n\nlet text = \"Hello W3Schools\";\n\nlet result = pattern.test(text); // false",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_hat"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "RegExp $ Metacharacter"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The $ metacharacter matches the end of a string."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const pattern = /W3Schools$/;\n\nlet text = \"Hello W3Schools\";\n\nlet result = pattern.test(text); // true",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const pattern = /W3Schools$/;\n\nlet text = \"W3Schools tutorial\";\n\nlet result = pattern.test(text); // false",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_regexp_dollar"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Learn More:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "JavaScript RegExp Assertions"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript RegExp Character Classes"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "// Match Digits\n\nconst pattern = /[0-9]/;",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Character Classes are characters enclosed in square brackets []."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "A character class matches any character from a set within brackets."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "These are the most common:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Class",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "[a]",
     "Matches the character between the brackets"
    ],
    [
     "[abc]",
     "Matches all characters between the brackets"
    ],
    [
     "[a-z]",
     "Matches all characters in the range from a to z"
    ],
    [
     "[0-9]",
     "Matches all characters in the range from 0 to 9"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let text = \"More than 1000 times\";\n\nconst pattern = /[0-9]/g;\n\nlet result = text.match(pattern);",
   "caption": "Example [0-9]"
  },
